I vote yes, as this appears to be structured to allow clarification,
etc, with minimal impact on stability.

The various contradictions in baselined documents (and there aren't
really very many of these (contradictions or documents, heh heh),
but long-distance vo'a and such things could certainly use an
official stamp) are worth sorting out, and there are probably one
or two things worth considering for official status (mu'ei, official
statement that sumtcita quantifier scope goes from the sumti to the
tag, maybe a few other minor things), along with getting more verbose
definitions.

I'd also like to get on the mailing list for byfy stuff whenever
that gets set up.

